This package builds on defog-adapt (frozen-base adapters, adapter composition, Feynman-Kac steering, inpainting and
the molecular domain code for DeFoG), which is itself derived from DeFoG:

    Yiming Qin, Manuel Madeira, Dorina Thanou, Pascal Frossard.
    "DeFoG: Discrete Flow Matching for Graph Generation." ICML 2025.
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.04263
    https://github.com/qym7/DeFoG

The credits and the papers behind each of those methods are listed in the NOTICE of defog-adapt.

The explainer side is MEGAN and its global concept explanations:

    Jonas Teufel, Luca Torresi, Patrick Reiser, Pascal Friederich.
    "MEGAN: Multi-explanation Graph Attention Network." xAI 2023, CCIS 1902, pp. 338-360.

    Jonas Teufel, Pascal Friederich.
    "Global Concept Explanations for Graphs by Contrastive Learning." xAI 2024, CCIS 2153, pp. 184-208.

The models of the model zoo were trained on data that carries its own terms (synthetic colored graphs generated by
code, ZINC, ChEMBL and the Ames mutagenicity benchmark). The model cards state them, and the zoo does not
redistribute the molecule tables.
